{{- if not (hasKey $sizes .workflow_size) -}}{{- fail (printf "workflow_size: unknown size %s" .workflow_size) -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $tiers := list -}}
{{- range $tier, $_ := .subagent_tiers.pi -}}{{- if ne $tier "frontier" -}}{{- $tiers = append $tiers $tier -}}{{- end -}}{{- end -}}
Launch plain JavaScript in an isolated VM; returns a background workflow id immediately, then the script's return value as JSON. title names the run's row. Keep trivial work inline and isolated bounded delegations on subagent; with ultracode on, use workflows for substantive multi-part work, including initially independent investigations needing reconciliation.{{/* model: Flat fan-out hides the reconciliation dependency between initially independent investigations. */}} A workflow is stages: later agents verify, reconcile or synthesise earlier results and the script returns the distilled result. For a staging shape or an execute-mode example, load the `workflow-authoring` skill. Ultracode is on if the <workflow> system-prompt section says so or the latest user prompt says ultracode. Launch is refused when off; management still works.

Manage with {action: "status", id?} to list runs or inspect one, {action: "result", id} to retrieve its outcome, or {action: "stop", id} to stop it. Only one workflow may be active at a time.

The script reaches only:
- agent(prompt, { agentType, tier?, schema?, label?, phase? }): resolves to the child's final text, or schema-validated value (JSON Schema); rejects on child failure. agentType comes from subagent's list. tier overrides its pin: {{ $tiers | join ", " }}; default is its own tier; frontier is refused. label titles its row; phase overrides phase(). model, effort and isolation are refused.
- phase(title): default heading for later agent() calls, not a dependency; use await.
- parallel([() => agent(...), ...]): runs the thunks concurrently; results in order, null where one failed.
- pipeline(items, ...stages): each item runs through stage(previous, item, index) on its own, with no barrier between stages; null where a stage failed.
- log(message): a progress line, cut at 2,000 characters; return the result from the script.
- args: the call's args value.
A leading `export const meta = {...}` is ignored. Nothing else is reachable: no files, shell, network, timers or modules.

Notes:
- Keep a run under {{ get $sizes .workflow_size }} agents unless the prompt asks for breadth.
- Root steering does not rewrite the script; steer named children via subagent controls. Root Escape/Ctrl+Enter interrupts the root, not the workflow; use stop to cancel it.
